(setter_cal -- measure the setter against the current work Z zero)

(Probes the setter and stores D, the trigger height in the active work)
(coordinate system. D is a property of the setup rather than of the tool, so)
(any later tool can be zeroed from it. Requires a correct Z zero; setter_zero)
(is the inverse operation.)

(D is stored in the G59.3 origin, which persists across restarts: #5383 holds)
(D and #5381 = 1 marks it valid. D is negative when the workpiece top sits)
(above the trigger height, so a nonzero test is not sufficient.)

o<setter_cal> sub

  M70

  o<setter_probe> call

  G10 L2 P9 X1 Z#5063

  (debug, setter calibrated: D = #5383 mm above work Z zero)

  G53 G0 Z#<_ini[TOOLSENSOR]SAFE_Z>

  M72

o<setter_cal> endsub
